### ARCHITECTURE FLOW
Player → Equipment → Session → Match → Rack → Shot → Events → Metrics → Skills → Statistics → Coach → Training → Dashboard → Career

### GOLDEN RULES
- Events = What happened
- Metrics = How often
- Skills = How good
- Coach = What to improve
- Training = How to improve
- Dashboard = Current ability
- Career = Long-term growth

## RFC-010 - Coach Intelligence Engine (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Coach AI MUST generate recommendations from real user data.
- Coach AI MUST NOT use hardcoded recommendations.
- If data is insufficient, Coach MUST return: `"Chưa có đủ dữ liệu để đưa ra khuyến nghị."`

### Data Flow
```
Player → Daily Readiness → Session → Match → Rack → Shot → Event
    → Statistics Engine → Coach Rule Engine → Coach Recommendation
```

### Coach Rule Engine
- Coach NEVER reads Session directly.
- Coach ALWAYS reads Statistics.
- Statistics are generated from Session → Rack → Shot → Event.

### Rule Categories
- Readiness: Should user train? Training intensity? Recovery needed?
- Skill Priority: Weakest skill, most improved, regression
- Match Review: Why won/lost, largest mistake/strength
- Equipment: Cue/tip impact
- Mental: Pressure, confidence, rush, focus, hill-hill
- Training Plan: Warmup, main drill, match practice, cooldown

### Coach Output Format
Every recommendation MUST contain:
1. Observation
2. Evidence
3. Recommendation
4. Expected Improvement

### Acceptance Criteria
- Coach explains WHY, WHAT, HOW, EXPECTED RESULT
- If Statistics are insufficient, MUST NOT generate fake advice

## RFC-011 - Session Data Collection Specification (REQUIRED)

### Data Hierarchy
```
Player → Session → Match → Rack → Shot (Optional) → Event
```

### Session Screen Required Fields
- Session Name, Session Type, Location, Table, Cloth, Ball Set, Date, Start Time, End Time, Session Goal

### Match Screen Required Fields
- Opponent, Race To, Current Score, Match Result
- Optional: Opponent Level, Table Condition, Pressure Level, Notes

### Rack Screen Required Fields
- Rack Number, Win/Lose, Break By, Break Success, Run Out, Open Table, Balls Potted (0-9), Longest Run (0-9), Scratch, Foul
- Biggest Mistake (single select), Biggest Strength (single select), Confidence (1-5), Pressure, Optional Note (max 300 chars)

### End of Rack Flow
1. User presses Win or Lose
2. Popup: Balls Potted
3. Biggest Mistake
4. Biggest Strength
5. Confidence
6. Save → Next Rack
- Target input time: < 10 seconds per rack
- User must never answer more than 5 questions after one rack

### End of Match Display
- Match Result, Rack Score, Win Rate, Break Success, Longest Run, Biggest Mistake, Biggest Strength, Coach Summary

### End of Session Generate
- Session Summary, Statistics, Coach Recommendation, Training Suggestion, Recovery Suggestion

## RFC-012 - Statistics Engine Specification (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Coach AI MUST ONLY read Statistics.
- Coach AI MUST NEVER read raw Session data directly.

### Statistics Categories
1. Overall Performance
2. Break Performance
3. Potting Performance
4. Position Play
5. Safety
6. Cue Ball Control
7. Mental
8. Equipment
9. Trend
10. Training

### Required Statistics
- Overall: Matches Played/Won/Lost, Rack Won/Lost, Win Rate, Average Match/Rack Duration, Average Balls Per Rack, Longest Run, Current/Longest Winning Streak
- Break: Break Attempts, Successful Break, Dry Break, Scratch On Break, Break Success %, Average Balls After Break, Break And Run, Golden Break, Power/Control Break %
- Potting: Balls Potted, Pot Success %, Long/Thin Cut/Rail/Combination/Bank/Kick/Jump Success %
- Position: Position Success %, Good/Bad Position, Too Long/Short, Wrong Angle, Lost Shape, Average Position Rating
- Cue Ball Control: Cue Ball Accuracy, Scratch Rate, Draw/Follow/Stop Success, Spin Accuracy, Speed Control
- Safety: Safety Attempts, Successful/Failed Safety, Safety Success/Escape %, Kick Escape %
- Mental: Confidence Average, Pressure/Hill-Hill Win %, Focus Rating, Rush/Tilt Events, Recovery After Miss
- Equipment: Current Cue/Shaft/Tip, Equipment Usage Time, Performance By Tip/Shaft/Cue, Equipment Change Impact
- Trend: Last 3/5/10 Sessions, 30/90 Days, Lifetime - every statistic includes trend (Improving/Stable/Declining)
- Skill Radar: Break, Shot Making, Position, Safety, Cue Ball Control, Mental, Consistency (0-100)
- Consistency Score: 0-100 based on Position, Potting, Mental, Break, Scratch, Foul
- Readiness: Average Sleep/Energy/Stress/Recovery, Training Load, Recovery Score, Readiness Trend
- Session Statistics: Duration, Total Matches/Racks, Win %, Average Balls, Biggest Strength/Weakness, Coach Summary
- Match Statistics: Rack Timeline, Momentum, Longest Run, Key Mistake, Turning Point, Pressure Performance
- Rack Statistics: Balls, Mistake, Strength, Confidence, Pressure, Events
- Player Statistics: Lifetime/Weekly/Monthly/Yearly, Best/Worst Session, Current Trend, Potential Improvement
- Dashboard Statistics: Today's Readiness, Current Focus, Skill Radar, Weekly Hours, Last Session, Coach Recommendation, Current Equipment, Training Progress

### Required Output for Every Statistic
- Current Value, Trend, Target, History

### Update Rules
- Statistics MUST update immediately after Rack Save, Match Save, Session Save

### Acceptance Criteria
- Every Session/Match/Rack generates statistics
- Statistics support Coach Engine
- Dashboard uses Statistics only
- No hardcoded values
- Every statistic supports trend analysis and historical comparison

## RFC-013 - Coach Rule Library (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Coach MUST generate recommendations from predefined rules only.
- Coach MUST NEVER randomly generate advice.
- Every recommendation MUST be supported by Statistics.

### Rule Priority
1. Health
2. Readiness
3. Mental
4. Skill Weakness
5. Training Plan
6. Equipment

### Coach Output Format
Every recommendation MUST include:
1. Observation
2. Evidence
3. Recommendation
4. Expected Result

### Key Rule Groups
- Readiness: Ready Score thresholds → Heavy/Normal/Light/Recovery training
- Sleep: <5h reduce volume, <4h no match practice, >7h normal
- Stress: >=8 → no pressure drill, focus technique only
- Confidence: <=2 avoid competition, >=4 pressure drill allowed
- Break: <50% success → break/power control/cue ball control drills
- Thin Cut: <60% → thin cut/ghost ball/reference drills
- Long Pot: <55% → long straight/long cut/distance control drills
- Position: <65% → stop/follow/draw shot, position ladder
- Cue Ball Control: scratch >10% → speed/center ball/stop drills
- Safety: <60% → safety/distance/thin safety drills
- Kick: <50% → 1-rail/2-rail kick, diamond system
- Bank: <40% → cross/long/short bank drills
- Hill-Hill: lose > win → pressure/routine/breathing drills
- Consistency: <70 → reduce difficulty, increase repetition
- Equipment: performance drop after tip change → continue testing or revert
- Fatigue: >5 consecutive training days → recovery day
- Regression: skill drops 3 sessions → high priority training
- Improvement: skill rises 5 sessions → reduce volume, move to next weakest skill
- Training Distribution: Weak 50%, Medium 30%, Strong 20%
- No Recommendation: insufficient statistics → `"Chưa đủ dữ liệu để đưa ra khuyến nghị."`

### Acceptance Criteria
- Recommendations are data-driven, consistent, explainable, repeatable
- No random output
- No hardcoded recommendation
- All recommendations generated from Statistics and Rule Engine only

## RFC-014 - Training Drill Library (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Coach MUST recommend real drills, NEVER only a skill name.
- Every drill has measurable goals.
- Every drill belongs to one Skill.
- Every Skill contains multiple Drills.

### Drill Categories
1. Warmup
2. Straight Shot
3. Thin Cut
4. Thick Cut
5. Long Pot
6. Position
7. Cue Ball Control
8. Break
9. Safety
10. Kick
11. Bank
12. Jump
13. Pattern Play
14. Pressure
15. Tournament
16. Mental
17. Recovery

### Drill Structure
Every drill contains: Drill ID, Name, Category, Difficulty, Skill, Description, Equipment Needed, Duration, Target, Evaluation, Coach Notes

### Difficulty Levels
- Beginner
- Intermediate
- Advanced
- Professional

### Sample Drills
- Warmup: W001 Center Ball Straight Shot, W002 Cue Ball Stop, W003 Distance Control
- Thin Cut: TC001 Short Thin Cut, TC002 Long Thin Cut, TC003 Rail Thin Cut
- Long Pot: LP001 Long Straight, LP002 Long Cut, LP003 Long Distance Follow
- Position: P001 Stop Shot, P002 Follow Shot, P003 Draw Shot, P004 Ladder Drill, P005 Clock Position Drill
- Cue Ball Control: CB001 Speed Control, CB002 Cue Ball Ladder, CB003 One Rail Position, CB004 Two Rail Position
- Break: B001 Power Break, B002 Control Break, B003 Wing Ball Practice, B004 Cue Ball Control After Break
- Safety: S001 Distance Safety, S002 Thin Safety, S003 Two Rail Safety
- Kick: K001 One Rail Kick, K002 Two Rail Kick, K003 Diamond System
- Bank: BK001 Cross Bank, BK002 Long Bank, BK003 Short Bank
- Jump: J001 Easy Jump, J002 Rail Jump
- Pattern: PT001 3 Ball Pattern, PT002 5 Ball Pattern, PT003 Run Out Pattern
- Pressure: PR001 Hill Hill Drill, PR002 Race To 5, PR003 Must Make Shot
- Mental: M001 Pre-shot Routine, M002 Breathing Routine, M003 Confidence Reset
- Recovery: R001 Shoulder Stretch, R002 Back Stretch, R003 Eye Relaxation

### Coach Recommendation Mapping Examples
- Position Accuracy <65% → P001, P002, P004
- Thin Cut Accuracy <60% → TC001, TC002, TC003
- Break Success <50% → B001, B002, B004
- High Stress → M001, M002, R001
- Ready Score <50 → Recovery only, no intensive drills

### Training Plan Generator
Example: Warmup 10 min → Thin Cut 20 min → Position 20 min → Pressure 15 min → Cooldown 5 min = Total 70 min

### Expected Improvement
Every Drill MUST define Expected Improvement, e.g.:
- Stop Shot → Position Accuracy, Cue Ball Control
- Thin Cut → Thin Cut Accuracy, Confidence
- Power Break → Break Success, Cue Ball Control

### Acceptance Criteria
- Coach NEVER recommends only a skill
- Coach ALWAYS recommends drills
- Every Drill has measurable goals
- Training plans are automatically generated from Statistics and Rule Engine

## RFC-015 - Coach Recommendation Engine (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Generate personalized daily training plans.
- Coach MUST combine Readiness * Statistics * Rule Engine * Training Library → Training Plan
- Coach MUST NEVER recommend drills randomly.

### Input
Player, Daily Readiness, Equipment, Current Session, Statistics, Trend, Rule Engine Output, Training Library

### Recommendation Pipeline
Daily Readiness → Statistics → Rule Engine → Skill Priority → Training Drill Selection → Training Schedule → Coach Message

### Steps
1. Readiness Check: Sleep, Energy, Stress, Confidence, Recovery → Training Level (Heavy/Normal/Light/Recovery)
2. Skill Priority: rank every skill, highest priority = weakest skill
3. Weakest Skill Selection: select top 3 weakest skills
4. Drill Selection: every skill has Easy/Medium/Hard, choose based on Player Level, Readiness, Current Trend
5. Training Time Distribution: Heavy 90-120 min, Normal 60-90 min, Light 30-45 min, Recovery 15-30 min
   - Weak Skill 50%, Medium 30%, Strong 20%

### Session Structure
Warmup → Main Drill → Secondary Drill → Pressure Drill → Cooldown

### Rules
- Warmup: always included, 5-10 min
- Pressure Drill: only if Readiness > 70 AND Confidence > 3, otherwise skip
- Mental: Stress > 7 → reduce difficulty, no pressure drill, recommend breathing routine
- Recovery: Sleep < 5h → no intensive drills, stretching, stop shot, recovery only
- Equipment: tip changed → do not recommend advanced drills, recommend calibration drills
- Regression: skill decreases 3 consecutive sessions → increase drill frequency
- Improvement: skill improves 5 consecutive sessions → reduce volume, move to next weakest skill

### Recommendation Limits
- Maximum 5 drills per day
- Never recommend more than 2 difficult drills in one session

### Weekly Rotation
- Avoid repeating same drill more than 3 consecutive sessions

### Adaptive Recommendation
- Adapt based on: Player Level, Current Trend, Equipment, Fatigue, Mental State, Recent Sessions

### Coach Explanation
Every recommendation MUST explain:
1. Observation
2. Evidence
3. Why this drill
4. Expected Improvement

### Recommendation History
Store: Date, Recommendation, Completed, Skipped, Success Rate
Coach uses history to avoid repetition.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Training plans are personalized
- Training intensity adapts daily
- Recommendations are data-driven
- No repeated drills
- No random output
- Coach always explains WHY

## RFC-016 - Dashboard & KPI Specification (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Dashboard is the Home Screen of Pool OS.
- Dashboard must answer 5 questions immediately:
  1. How am I today?
  2. What should I train?
  3. Am I improving?
  4. What is my biggest weakness?
  5. What should I do next?
- Dashboard MUST NOT become a statistics page.
- Dashboard MUST focus on action.

### Dashboard Sections
1. Daily Readiness
2. Coach Card
3. Today's Training
4. Skill Radar
5. Quick Statistics
6. Recent Sessions
7. Equipment Status
8. Weekly Progress

### Section Details
- Daily Readiness: Ready Score 0-100, color-coded (Green/Yellow/Orange/Red), Sleep/Energy/Stress/Confidence/Recovery, Coach Comment
- Coach Card: Today's Focus (max 120 chars), Coach Message, "View Full Coach Report" button
- Today's Training: Warmup, Main Drill, Secondary Drill, Pressure Drill, Cooldown, Estimated Time, Completion %, "Start Training" button
- Skill Radar: Break, Shot Making, Position, Safety, Cue Ball Control, Mental, Consistency (0-100), tap to open detail
- Quick Statistics: Win Rate, Rack Win %, Break Success, Position Accuracy, Thin Cut Accuracy, Longest Run, Current Streak, Weekly Hours
- Recent Sessions: last 5 sessions with Result, Duration, Coach Score, tap for detail
- Equipment: Current Cue/Shaft/Tip, Usage Time, Replacement Reminder
- Weekly Progress: Training Hours, Completed Drills, Coach Score, Improvement %, Weekly Goal, Completion %

### Dashboard KPI
- Ready Score, Coach Score, Skill Score, Trend Score
- Weekly Progress, Monthly Progress, Lifetime Progress

### Trend Indicators
Every KPI MUST show: Current Value, Trend, History
- Green = Improving, Yellow = Stable, Red = Declining, Grey = Insufficient Data

### Coach Score
Calculated from: Readiness, Statistics, Training Completion, Trend → 0-100

### Dashboard Refresh
Updates after: Session Save, Match Save, Rack Save, Daily Check-in, Equipment Change

### Empty State
If no data: Welcome → Create First Session → Start Practice
- No fake statistics.

### Performance
- Dashboard loading < 1 second
- Statistics loaded asynchronously
- Charts cached

### Acceptance Criteria
- Dashboard shows today's status immediately
- Coach recommendation visible without entering other screens
- All KPI calculated from Statistics Engine
- No hardcoded values
- Every widget supports Vietnamese
- Every card can be tapped for details

## RFC-017 - Complete User Workflow Specification (REQUIRED)

### Core Rules
- Every screen must have a complete workflow.
- Application MUST NEVER leave user without a next action.
- Every button must have a destination.
- Every action must update database.
- Every completed workflow must refresh Dashboard.

### Main Navigation
Dashboard → Session → Statistics → Equipment → Player → Settings

### Workflows
- Player: Dashboard → Player → Player List → Add Player → Save → Refresh → Back; Edit/Delete with confirmation
- Equipment: Equipment → Cue List → Add/Edit/Delete Cue → Refresh; Tip/Shaft search and save
- Session: Dashboard → New Session → Fill Info → Save → Open Session Detail → Create Match → Save → Open Match
- Match: Match Detail → Start Match → Rack 1...N → Final Rack → Match Summary → Save → Back To Session
- Rack: Rack Screen → Play Rack → Win/Lose → Popup Summary → Balls Potted → Biggest Mistake → Biggest Strength → Confidence → Save → Next Rack
- End Match: Last Rack → Match Result → Statistics Update → Coach Analysis → Return Session
- End Session: Finish Session → Session Summary → Statistics Update → Coach Report → Dashboard Refresh
- Dashboard: Open App → Readiness → Dashboard Refresh → Coach Card → Today's Training → Recent Session
- Coach: Dashboard → Coach Card → Open Coach → Today's Recommendation → Training Plan → Start Training
- Statistics: Dashboard → Statistics → Overview → Skill → Trend → Session History → Match History → Rack History
- Daily Readiness: Open App → Daily Check → Sleep/Energy/Stress/Confidence → Save → Dashboard Refresh → Coach Refresh

### Required Confirmation
Delete Player, Delete Cue, Delete Session, Delete Match, Delete Rack → Always ask confirmation

### Dashboard Refresh Rules
Refresh after: Player Update, Equipment Update, Readiness Update, Rack Save, Match Save, Session Save, Coach Analysis, Statistics Update

### Empty States
- No Player → Create Player
- No Equipment → Add Cue
- No Session → Start Practice
- No Statistics → Complete First Session

### Error Handling
- Database Error → Retry/Cancel
- Validation Error → Highlight Missing Fields
- Network Error → Offline Mode

### Loading Rules
- Every Save → Loading Indicator
- Every Success → Success Message
- Every Failure → Error Message

### Acceptance Criteria
- Every button performs an action
- No dead-end screens
- No empty navigation
- Dashboard always refreshes automatically
- Coach always refreshes after Session
- Statistics always refresh after Match
- Every workflow completed without returning to Home manually

